   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Dolly Zoom\n\nThe vertigo shot: a corridor with a red door stretches deeper while the subject in the middle keeps its exact size. A host puts its own subject in by replacing the .dz-subject svg with its own centered content.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 2.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A realization or a turning point in the story needs one unsettling, cinematic beat.\n- A logo, product or figure should stay perfectly still while the space around it warps.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need to move from one scene to the next, not a held shot: use push-through.\n- The move should feel calm and simply show depth: use parallax-depth.\n\nVariables:\n- intensity (number, 0-2): Intensity, default 1\n- reverse (boolean): Reverse, default false\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#0B0B0B\"\n- wall_color (color): Wall, default \"#1B1B1B\"\n- wall_alt_color (color): Wall alt, default \"#151515\"\n- floor_color (color): Floor, default \"#262626\"\n- floor_alt_color (color): Floor alt, default \"#1D1D1D\"\n- line_color (color): Lines, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- light_color (color): Ceiling lights, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- door_color (color): Door, default \"#E5322D\"\n- figure_color (color): Figure, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
